ptual","question":"What kind of constants are required for strongly equivalent metrics?","options":["Positive constants","Negative constants","Only the constant $0$","Complex constants"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"d74bd5d35423ee708fc238e5"},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_strongly_equivalent_metrics_ec12ec7b_003","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"If $d_q(x,y) = 3d_p(x,y)$ for all $x,y\\in X$, which constants show $d_p\\approx d_q$?","options":["$a = 0$, $b = 3$","$a = -3$, $b = 3$","$a = 1$, $b = 1$ only","$a = 3$, $b = 3$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"3023de6bacdba8fcda741696"},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_strongly_equivalent_metrics_ec12ec7b_004","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"Which pair of metrics is strongly equivalent?","options":["The discrete metric and any $p$-metric","Any two unrelated functions on $X$","Any two $p$-metrics on $\\mathbb{R}^n$","A metric and a non-metric distance rule"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"9d997b3c6c1e905988a35f56"},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_strongly_equivalent_metrics_ec12ec7b_005","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Which property holds for strong equivalence of metrics?","options":["Non-differentiability","Transitivity","Non-reflexivity","Failure of symmetry"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"412373912bbffa2f70c9e052"},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_strongly_equivalent_metrics_ec12ec7b_006","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"What notion is preserved by strongly equivalent metrics?","options":["Matrix multiplication","Polynomial degree","Endpoint convergence of power series","Convergence"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"2e5de26176b4416c1f244db1"},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_strongly_equivalent_metrics_ec12ec7b_007","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"Suppose $2d_p(x,y)\\leq d_q(x,y)\\ \\leq 5d_p(x,y)$ for all $x,y\\in X$. What can be concluded?","options":["$d_p$ is not a metric","$d_q$ is not a metric","$d_p\\approx d_q$","The metrics induce different notions of convergence"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"dbced599f9a877fb6b0ec497"},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_strongly_equivalent_metrics_ec12ec7b_008","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"If $d_p\\approx d_q$ and a sequence converges under $d_p$, what follows?","options":["It must diverge under $d_q$","It becomes eventually constant","It stops being a sequence in $X$","It also converges under $d_q$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"78a4f63cd8d4733f916ff676"},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_strongly_equivalent_metrics_ec12ec7b_009","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"conceptual","question":"How can symmetry of strong equivalence be seen from $a d_p\\leq d_q\\leq b d_p$?","options":["It implies $\\frac{1}{b}d_q\\leq d_p\\leq\\frac{1}{a}d_q$","It implies $d_p = d_q$ exactly","It requires $a = b = 0$","It only works when $X$ has one point"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"85550cfaebeac90b10b29204"},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_strongly_equivalent_metrics_ec12ec7b_010","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"conceptual","question":"If $d_p\\approx d_q$ and $d_q\\approx d_r$, what property gives $d_p\\approx d_r$?","options":["Transitivity","Reflexivity only","Endpoint checking","Uniform convergence"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"28c04873c95ded5794d368c7"},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_strongly_equivalent_metrics_ec12ec7b_011","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"application","question":"Suppose $a d_p\\leq d_q\\leq b d_p$ and $c d_q\\leq d_r\\leq e d_q$ for positive constants. Which constants can bound $d_r$ in terms of $d_p$?","options":["$ac$ and $be$","$a+c$ and $b+e$","$a/e$ and $b/c$","$0$ and $1$ only"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"5f5dcba24caf1e20198653fc"},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_strongly_equivalent_metrics_ec12ec7b_012","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"application","question":"Which comparison fails for the discrete metric versus a usual $p$-metric on $\\mathbb{R}^n$?","options":["The discrete metric cannot measure distance between points.","No global constants bound the two metrics above and below.","The usual $p$-metric is undefined on $\\mathbb{R}^n$.","Both metrics always give exactly the same numerical distance."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"dd12729610c2a4e85b00b12f"},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_strongly_equivalent_metrics_ec12ec7b_013","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"What inequality defines strong equivalence of metrics $d_p$ and $d_q$?","options":["$d_p(x,y)=d_q(x,y)$ for all $x,y$ only.","$a d_p(x,y)\\le d_q(x,y)\\le b d_p(x,y)$ for some $a,b \\gt 0$","$d_p(x,y)\\le 0\\le d_q(x,y)$","$d_p(x,y)+d_q(x,y)=1$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"65d9b635b6f07892b85bf447"},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_strongly_equivalent_metrics_ec12ec7b_014","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"What kind of constants are used for strong equivalence?","options":["Negative constants only","A single constant equal to $0$","Constants depending on $x$ and $y$","Positive constants $a$ and $b$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"08111888e11d4e187f35675a"},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_strongly_equivalent_metrics_ec12ec7b_015","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Which notation denotes strong equivalence of $d_p$ and $d_q$?","options":["$d_p=d_q=0$","$d_p\\in d_q$","$d_p\\approx d_q$","$d_p\\cup d_q$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"5f3c18da00592635f3c36b95"},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_strongly_equivalent_metrics_ec12ec7b_016","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"If $2d_p(x,y)\\le d_q(x,y)\\le 5d_p(x,y)$ for all $x,y$, what can be concluded?","optio